From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Serve opset-28 type-only schema updates with the existing CPU kernels

conda-forge only.  ONNX 1.23 gives 19 ai.onnx operators a new schema
version at opset 28.  onnxruntime 1.30.0 plus the backport of
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/pull/32359 (patch 0013) has
opset-28 kernels for two of them, Mod and BitShift.  For the rest, the
newest CPU kernel is registered open-ended ("since version N"), and
KernelRegistry::VerifyVersion only lets an open-ended kernel serve a node
whose schema version equals N.  Any opset-28 model using one of them
therefore fails to load:

    Failed to find kernel for Cast(28) ... Version mismatch.
    node_version: 28 kernel start version: 25
    kernel_end_version: 2147483647

Upstream did not see this because ONNX 1.23.0 and 1.23.1 still report
opset 27 as the last released one (https://github.com/onnx/onnx/issues/8529),
so models built at the default opset stayed on 27.  The conda-forge
libonnx 1.23.1 carries the fix for that, which moves the default to 28
and makes 24 onnxruntime unit tests (MoETest, CausalConvWithStateTest,
and on macOS a CoreML test) fail on the missing Cast(28) kernel.

For the operators whose opset-28 schema differs from the previous one
only in its type constraints, the existing kernel implements the opset-28
operator for every type it already supports.  Give those registrations
an explicit end version of 28 so they serve both schema versions:

    Cast (25), Celu (12), Compress (11), DepthToSpace (13),
    DequantizeLinear (25), QuantizeLinear (25), Einsum (12), OneHot (11),
    Optional (15), OptionalHasElement (18), OptionalGetElement (18),
    ReduceLogSum (18), ReduceLogSumExp (18), ReverseSequence (10),
    Unique (11)

The types opset 28 adds (bfloat16, float6e2m3, float6e3m2, and the wider
Optional/Celu lists) are NOT implemented by this patch; such models are
rejected for a missing kernel as before.  ReduceLogSum/ReduceLogSumExp
lose their integer types in opset 28; the integer kernels are extended
with the others and are simply never selected for an opset-28 node.

Deliberately left alone:

  * SpaceToDepth -- opset 28 adds a `mode` attribute the kernel does not
    implement; registering it would silently compute the wrong result
    for mode=CRD.  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/pull/32362
  * SwiGLU -- new operator.
    https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/pull/32381
  * the CUDA and other execution providers -- an opset-28 node of these
    operators is assigned to the CPU kernel instead.

Upstream's own per-operator opset-28 work is in the open pull requests
32362, 32372, 32378, 32381 and 32393; drop this patch when onnxruntime
ships them.
